    "content": "All 19 checklist items have been tested and recorded — coverage is complete.\n\n**Summary: 8 PASS / 11 FAIL**\n\nPassing: search & filtering (FT-1), opening model details (FT-2), node dragging (FT-3), template library browsing (FT-6), scenario switching (FT-9), immediate coverage/progress updates (IX-13), the directed weighted graph presentation (CT-15), and risk-gap detection & alerting (CT-17, CT-18).\n\nThe failures cluster around three root defects:\n1. **Stale graph node rendering** — node controls never reflect edits (level, weight, disabled state), and any subsequent edit is applied to stale data, silently reverting earlier changes (FT-4, FT-5, FT-7, IX-20).\n2. **Analysis inconsistency** — the critical-path summary includes disabled competencies, isn't a valid graph path, and disagrees with graph highlighting (CT-16).\n3. **Missing/faulty persistence and simulation validation** — Save and Save-Current only show toasts without storing anything (FT-8, FT-11), the initially selected scenario loads with zeroed adjustments (IX-19), and minimum category-slider values corrupt sibling adjustments into NaN, producing \"NaN%\" coverage and out-of-range weights (FT-10, CS-12)."
